  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MAAN-DANIDA SP OPTI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MA&apos;AN will lead on Change Objective 2 in the Gaza Strip. MA&apos;AN will achieve the expected outcome through the implementation of three main interlinked strategies, in the following sequence:
During Year 1:
- Build the capacities of crisis-affected young women graduates (22-24 yrs.) on Green agri TVET skills. MA&apos;AN will announce opportunities for TVET to young women in the targeted area. Young women applicants will be invited to attend orientation sessions about MA&apos;AN&apos;s TVET programs provided at its Community Services Centerin Deir Al Balah in the Gaza Strip. A group of 60 applicants will be selected based on the agreed upon criterion: participants are graduates based in Beit Hanon or Deir Al Balah, aged 22-24 yrs.; applicants with agri-relevant educational backgrounds will be prioritised, especially young women with disabilities who meet these criteria. Beit Hanoun is the leading agricultural area in Gaza, as well as the most marginalized, as indicated in the market study conducted by Oxfam.  Ultimately, a total of 60 young participants will be selected and enrolled in TVET training in green and SMART agribusiness (60 training hours) (Activity 2.1.1-2.1.4). The trainings will be provided at MA&#x2019;AN&apos;s Community Services Center in Deir Al Balah (in Deir Al Balah Governorate and Bait Hanoun Area). The 60participants will also receive Entrepreneurship and Green Economy training (28 hours), and will be supported to contextualise and practice the acquired skills by participating in a two-day boot camp for group coaching sessions on the market system and value chains (Activities 2.2.1.-2.2.4).
During Year 2:
- Provide seed funding to entrepreneurial and innovative projects to integrate the youngwomen in the labour market. A total of 5 young participants, with promising business concepts, will be selected to receive the seedfunding and support package which consists of customised business skills training. The training will focus on developing their marketing, technical, and financial skills (10 hours for each), as well as the provision of mentoring by MA&#x2019;AN&apos;s pool of mentors (Activities 2.2.5).</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MA&apos;AN Development Center is an independent Palestinian development and training institution established in January,1989, registeredby law as a non-profit organization.  The main office is located in Ramallah and the four branch offices are located in Gaza, Khan Younis, Tulkarem  and Jenin,.  MA&apos;AN&apos;s work is informed by the necessity of creating independent, self-reliant initiatives that leadto the development of human resources for sustainable development, which incorporate values of self-sufficiency and self-empowerment.</narrative>
